# MCP servers this distribution knows how to install. Read by bin/oal-mcp-*.
#
# Format, pipe-separated:  id | kind | package | args | visibility | profiles | description
#
#   kind      uvx (Python, run by uv) or npx (Node). Both are already installed by
#             install/agentarchy-base.packages, so neither adds a dependency.
#   args      arguments the server needs, or empty. $HOME is the only expansion
#             permitted -- a data file that can expand arbitrary shell is a data file
#             that can run arbitrary shell.
#   visibility  public, private, hardware or commercial. Anything but public is skipped by a
#             profile install and reported with a reason, rather than attempted and failed --
#             a private registry, an absent instrument or a missing licence is not a bug to
#             surface as an install error. Naming such a server explicitly still installs it.
#   profiles  comma-separated; oal-mcp-install --profile takes one of these names.
#   package   the exact registry name. Every entry here was checked against
#             registry.npmjs.org or pypi.org before it was added -- a catalog whose
#             names are guesses is worse than no catalog, because the failure lands
#             on the user as an install error rather than on us as a missing row.
#
# Nothing in here is installed by default. The distribution ships the mechanism; what
# you run is your choice, and `oal-mcp-import` registers catalogs this repository does
# not ship (private, licence-gated, or hardware-bound) without them appearing here.
#
# Deliberately vendor-neutral: these are the reference servers and a few widely used
# ones, not a curated set that reflects one person's work. Opinionated defaults are
# good; an opinionated *catalogue* is a lock-in.

filesystem | npx | @modelcontextprotocol/server-filesystem | $HOME | public | minimal,dev | Read and write files under paths you name
git | uvx | mcp-server-git |  | public | minimal,dev | Read, search and inspect a git repository
fetch | uvx | mcp-server-fetch |  | public | minimal,dev | Retrieve a URL and convert it to text
time | uvx | mcp-server-time |  | public | minimal,dev | Current time and timezone conversion
memory | npx | @modelcontextprotocol/server-memory |  | public | dev | A knowledge graph the agent can persist notes into
sequential-thinking | npx | @modelcontextprotocol/server-sequential-thinking |  | public | dev | Structured step-by-step reasoning
github | npx | @modelcontextprotocol/server-github |  | public | dev | Issues, pull requests and code search on GitHub
sqlite | uvx | mcp-server-sqlite |  | public | dev | Query and inspect a SQLite database
playwright | npx | @playwright/mcp |  | public | dev | Drive a real browser: navigate, click, read, screenshot
context7 | npx | @upstash/context7-mcp |  | public | dev | Up-to-date library and framework documentation
